<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Tauri merges this file into the generated app bundle's Info.plist.

  Only one key so far, and it is here for a concrete reason: roadmap #23's Live
  Photo export can hand the finished JPEG+MOV pair to the macOS Photos library
  (`lptool import`, src-tauri/native/livephoto/main.swift), which is the only
  path that actually produces a real Live Photo rather than two loose files.
  PhotoKit refuses to even show a permission prompt without this description —
  the process is killed instead — so without this key the feature cannot work.

  The wording is add-only on purpose, matching the `.addOnly` authorization the
  tool requests: Mazij never reads the user's existing photos.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>NSPhotoLibraryAddUsageDescription</key>
  <string>لإضافة الصور الحية التي تصدّرها من مزيج إلى مكتبة الصور. مزيج يضيف فقط ولا يقرأ صورك.</string>
</dict>
</plist>
